Hi there,

I'm fairly new to MSstats and was just wondering how features (I'm guessing peptide intensities) are used to calculate protein intensity?

I noticed such drastic results when using "all" vs. "top3" in dataProcess. Since I am analyzing human plasma, I noticed that in "all", the log2 intensities of ALBU_HUMAN across my samples were around 16-17, whereas in "top3", the log2 intensities were around 25-26. So does MSstats take the median of either "all" or "top3"? (I always thought it was the sum.)

Thank you,
Julie

