Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi:
I just want to make sure that what I am getting using MSStatsTMT is correct, meaning that I am doing it right.
I have a 16 plex TMT experiment, a single mixture, with samples from 3 biological subjects. Each of these samples from the subjects have been treated with 5 different compounds, therefore I have subject1 x 5 + subject2 x 5 + subject3 x 5 = 15 channels, plus an additional channel in which I mix the 3 subjects untreated together, which makes the 16 channels.
Then, using MSstatsTMT, I wanted to not only analyze the data comparing the 5 compounds versus the mix, which I do with no problems, but I wanted to get the individual comparisons of each channel vs the mix channel, meaning, to get the differentially expressed proteins between each subject with each treatment vs the mix with no treatment, which is a single channel vs a single channel.
However, when I do that using groupComparisonTMT function, using the moderate=TRUE, it fails due to an error because variance is zero, and if I use moderate=FALSE, it doesn't fail but all the results have the issue "SingleMeasurePerCondition".
Is there a way to get results comparing one channel vs one channel?
Thank you in advance.

Salva

